sequenceDiagram
    title Option A: APISIX handles the login (session cookie)
    participant B as Browser
    participant A as APISIX
    participant Z as Zitadel
    participant O as OPA
    participant N as Node app

    B->>A: GET /a/ (no session)
    A-->>B: 302 to Zitadel /oauth/v2/authorize (code + PKCE)
    B->>Z: login page, username + password
    Z-->>B: 302 to /a/callback?code=...
    B->>A: GET /a/callback?code=...
    A->>Z: POST /oauth/v2/token (code + client secret, server-side)
    Z-->>A: access, ID and refresh tokens
    A-->>B: 302 to /a/ + Set-Cookie: session (HttpOnly, encrypted)
    B->>A: POST /a/hello (cookie only)
    A->>A: decrypt session, add X-Access-Token / X-ID-Token / X-Userinfo
    A->>O: authz query (headers + route id)
    O->>O: server roles = data.server_roles[project][sub]
    alt writer role
        O-->>A: allow + X-Roles
        A->>N: forward with token headers + X-Roles
        N-->>B: 200
    else no writer role
        O-->>A: deny
        A-->>B: 403 writer role required
    end
